This directory holds compatibility files for hosting Larceny's build
process (Twobit, the assemblers, and the bootstrap heap dumper) under
modern Racket (tested with Racket v9.3 CS), using the plt-r5rs
language, which provides mutable pairs, mutable string literals, and
an R5RS-style top level.

The setup process mutates bindings in the standard environment
(e.g. load), so plt-r5rs must be started with the --no-prim flag:

  % plt-r5rs --no-prim
  > (load "setup.sch")
  > (setup 'scheme: 'racket 'host: 'macosx-arm64)
  > (build-config-files)
  > (load-compiler)
  ...

The older MzScheme and PLT-R5RS compatibility layers target PLT
Scheme v3/v4 and no longer work with current versions of Racket.
